It appears that since the introduction of MERIT v5.27 and turning on diagnostics being sent to MERIT that there are a significant number of messages ending up in ABT quarantine. We need to improve the process in CloudFare of filtering out which messages are sent to MERIT so that this doesn’t happen anymore.

The messages going to quarantine are like he below examples:

From Validator: {"MeritDDSRemoteEndpointAddress":null,"Shift":null,"Equipment":{"Id":0,"DeviceId":0,"ShiftId":null,"SerialNumber":"000080","DallasSerialNumber":null,"HomeLocation":0,"AllocatedLocation":null,"VehicleNumber":null,"OtherData":"1100000000001","PrimaryEquipment":null,"EquipmentType":14,"EquipmentTypeGroupId":6},"Device":null,"Journey":null,"HomeOperator":null,"Diagnostic":{"EventDate":"2025-03-18T12:14:49.446+00:00","EventCode":1415,"JourneyId":null,"ShiftId":null,"ServiceName":null,"PublicRouteCode":null}}

From Glider HHD: {"MeritDDSRemoteEndpointAddress":null,"Shift":null,"Equipment":{"Id":0,"DeviceId":0,"ShiftId":null,"SerialNumber":"","DallasSerialNumber":null,"HomeLocation":0,"AllocatedLocation":null,"VehicleNumber":null,"OtherData":null,"PrimaryEquipment":null,"EquipmentType":35,"EquipmentTypeGroupId":7},"Device":null,"Journey":{"EquipmentId":343878,"JourneyId":5740488,"ClientJourneyId":"caa0812d-b864-47ef-81b9-04582dc59efc","JourneyNumber":3527,"ShiftId":1436038,"ClientShiftId":"7fe9c961-a268-44df-8cbd-e7b6c32b5981","RouteVariantNumber":null,"Direction":1,"JourneyStartDateTime":"2025-03-18T12:14:22.801+00:00","PatternNumber":null,"FareboxId":null,"ServiceType":0,"ServiceOptionFlags":null,"EndDateTime":null,"CashTotal":null,"PassTotal":null,"TicketTotal":null,"DummyJourney":false},"HomeOperator":null,"Diagnostic":{"EventDate":"2025-03-18T12:15:28.02+00:00","EventCode":5001,"JourneyId":"caa0812d-b864-47ef-81b9-04582dc59efc","ShiftId":null,"ServiceName":"Glider Service","PublicRouteCode":"Glider"}}

If there is no ShiftId then the message should not be sent to MERIT. I believe this would stop both of these types of messages ending up in quarantine.
